.TH MCPRACK 1 "August 2026" "mcprack" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
mcprack \- command-line administration for the mcprack MCP server catalog
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mcprack
.RI [ --host " " HOST ]
.RI [ --port " " PORT ]
.br
.B mcprack
.I COMMAND
.RI [ ARGS ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mcprack
is a self-service catalog and client-config generator for Model Context
Protocol (MCP) servers. This command is a dual-mode launcher installed by
the Debian package:
.PP
With no arguments, or an argument starting with
.BR - ,
it starts the Flask development server (development/manual use only \-
production runs via
.B gunicorn
and the
.B mcprack.service
systemd unit):
.PP
.RS
mcprack --host 0.0.0.0 --port 8913
.RE
.PP
With any other first argument, it forwards to the Flask management CLI,
equivalent to running
.B "flask --app mcprack.app:create_app"
with the same arguments. This exposes the top-level
.BR create-admin ", " db " and " audit-archive
commands, plus the
.BR user ", " server " and " secret
command groups documented below.
.SH COMMANDS
.SS Top-level
.TP
.B create-admin
Create an initial admin account interactively.
.TP
.B db upgrade
Apply pending database migrations (Alembic, via Flask-Migrate).
.TP
.B db stamp head
Mark the database schema as up to date without running migrations.
.TP
.B audit-archive
Archive or prune old audit log entries. See
.B --help
for retention/output flags.
.SS user \- manage mcprack user accounts
.TP
.B user list
List all user accounts (id, username, auth type, email, admin/disabled flags).
.TP
.BI "user create " "[--username USERNAME] [--password PASSWORD] [--email EMAIL] [--admin]"
Create a local user account. Prompts for username/password if omitted.
.TP
.BI "user delete " "USERNAME " "--yes"
Permanently delete a user account and their selections/overrides.
Requires
.B --yes
confirmation.
.TP
.BI "user passwd " USERNAME
Reset a local user's password (fails for non-local auth types).
.TP
.BI "user enable " USERNAME
Re-enable a disabled user account.
.TP
.BI "user disable " USERNAME
Disable a user account, blocking login without deleting it.
.TP
.BI "user promote " USERNAME
Grant admin privileges to a user.
.TP
.BI "user demote " USERNAME
Revoke admin privileges from a user.
.SS server \- manage MCP catalog servers
.TP
.B server list
List all MCP catalog servers (id, name, transport, enabled/disabled, category).
.TP
.BI "server show " NAME
Show a server's non-secret configuration: label, transport, enabled state,
category, command/args or url, declared secret keys, and install method
if the server was installed via the pip/npm/docker installer subsystem.
.TP
.BI "server enable " NAME
Enable a server so users can select it in the catalog.
.TP
.BI "server disable " NAME
Disable a server, hiding it from the catalog.
.TP
.BI "server delete " "NAME " "--yes"
Permanently delete a server and any stored credentials. Requires
.B --yes
confirmation.
.SS secret \- manage a server's credential (secret env var) values
.TP
.B secret backend
Show which secret store backend is active: Vaultwarden, or the local
encrypted fallback (used when
.B BW_SERVER
is unset).
.TP
.BI "secret list " SERVER_NAME
List a server's declared secret env var keys and whether each currently
has a value set.
.TP
.BI "secret set " "SERVER_NAME KEY " "[--value VALUE]"
Set or overwrite one credential value for a server. Prompts for a hidden
value if
.B --value
is omitted.
.TP
.BI "secret unset " "SERVER_NAME KEY"
Remove one credential value from a server.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Create an admin user directly from the shell:
.B mcprack user create --username alice --admin
.TP
Take a broken server out of the catalog without deleting it:
.B mcprack server disable jenkins
.TP
Rotate a server's API token:
.B mcprack secret set jenkins JENKINS_TOKEN
.TP
Check which secret backend is active:
.B mcprack secret backend
.PP
Every command and subcommand accepts
.BR --help .
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/mcprack/env
Runtime configuration (database URI, secret key, Vaultwarden/LDAP
settings). Sourced before running
.B mcprack
as the
.B mcprack
system user; see
.B README.Debian
for the full variable reference.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR flask (1),
.I /usr/share/doc/mcprack/README.Debian
